              "text": "nyāyādhīśa is a compound of nyāya, \"rule, justice, judicial sentence\", and adhīśa, \"lord, master\" (MW). MW does not list the compound, so using it for a court judge is a modern pairing. Nyāya is built on ni- and the root √i, \"to go\" (CDIAL 7614)."
